questions.solution:
Intestine is acidic due to formation of $\mathrm{HCl}during digestion. Excessive acidity$ in the intestine creates problem of intestinal ulcer, gastric reflux and oesophagitis. The compound which reduced or neutralise acidity are called antacids.

\begin{aligned}
&$\mathrm{NaHCO}_3+\mathrm{HCl}$ \rightarrow $\mathrm{NaCl}+\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}+\mathrm{CO}_2$ \\
& $\mathrm{Mg}$($\mathrm{OH}$)_2+2 $\mathrm{HCl}$ \rightarrow $\mathrm{MgCl}_2+2 \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}$
\end{aligned}

